From 30634e652cd5f3d863cba9d33583eca226f8be61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:51:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] scene (cutscene) commands, script-class methods and
 waiting calls in the debug channel

GTA VI 1.0.2.1 makes a cutscene with one native (name hash, flags) and drives it through methods
of the script object that native returns (the by-ID call path). So:
 * ncall takes m+0x<rva> (a method called by address, checked to be a function start) and names of
   methods (`NAME m+0x<rva>` lines of the names file); wait=<secs> repeats a call every 100 ms until
   its first return slot is not 0; a call whose $variable is not set is not made;
 * every scene a script creates is remembered (the native named SCENE_CREATE): scene list;
 * scene use | new | ent | load | wait | start | state | stop | play, over the names SCENE_* of the
   names file (no title address in the code);
 * a scene created from the channel: the script heap is garbage collected and nothing holds the
   returned object (seen freed within 90 s in run nat4), so the scene's id is moved into a block of
   ours and the script object is left with id 0 (untested at this commit: run nat5);
 * peek takes a hexadecimal length.
Checked in the game (nat4, cell checkpoint): pos / tp with heading / time / date / tpsave / tpgo /
tpmarks, scene list, scene use + state, and SCENE_START on the mission's own ready scene.

